  "note": "Third arm of the 2026-08-17 in-game series, same pak, same surface, the user: ?bench=all&benchcar=caddy&procobj=0 — the runtime clutter layer OFF on top of the cheap fleet. Asked: is the runtime clutter (per-category ranges 08-10, species floor 08-11 — both AFTER the 08-09 baseline) the world-side cost?",
  "analysis": "NO measurable change against the caddy arm: gpu.pass ls-noon 5.6->5.6, sf-fog-dawn 4.5->4.5, lv-night 10.8->10.7, country-dusk 12.0->12.0, ls-rain-night 4.9->4.9, ganton-noon 9.1->9.2, strip-noon 6.2->6.2, ganton-night 11.4->9.3 (that arm's caddy row was the noisy one; 9.3 is in line with ganton-noon). Draws and triangles are IDENTICAL to the caddy arm on every scene (country-dusk 788/787 draws, 1.31M/1.29M tris) — so either the clutter costs nothing on the GPU pass, or the knob did not apply on this path (the HUD's clutter line / the [procobj] boot line would tell; the draw and triangle counts not moving at all is what makes the second reading plausible). Either way the runtime clutter is NOT where the x3 lives. What is left: the world's own drawn cost per pixel — same-ish geometry (country-dusk 1.3M tris, 787 draws vs 1.23M / 874 at the 08-09 baseline) costs 3x more GPU pass, and ocean-horizon (sky only) is unchanged, so the render target is the same size. That points at overdraw / alpha classes / texture footprint of what the cells carry now (cellVertex +35 % on country-dusk, texture +9 %), or the far LOD ring's content (2dfx at LOD range, the lod_* cells). NEXT: (a) ?bench=all&benchcar=caddy&draw=400 (LOD ring floored — if pass collapses, the far ring is the cost); (b) probe=0; (c) then the UNCAPPED headless lane and a rect-repack A/B against the pack input of a mod layer (Urbanize / 64 / 65) — model-repack.ts is the instrument for one model, opensa-pack --rect for an area.",
